   $q$Daily water use at a community garden is approximately normal with mean $150$ gallons and standard deviation $10$ gallons. A z-table gives $P(Z < 0.8) = 0.7881$. On about what percent of days does the garden use less than $142$ gallons?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$21.19\\%$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$28.81\\%$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"subtracted-one-half"},{"text":"$78.81\\%$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignored-negative-z"},{"text":"$57.62\\%$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"gave-middle-area"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$21.19\%$$q$, $q$$z = \frac{142 - 150}{10} = -0.8$. By symmetry $P(Z < -0.8) = 1 - 0.7881 = 0.2119$, about $21.19\%$. The choice $78.81\%$ uses $z = 0.8$ and forgets that $142$ is below the mean.$q$, 'draft', null)
