   $q$At one high school, 100 student volunteers were randomly assigned to use a new vocabulary app or to study with paper flashcards. After a month, the app group scored much higher, by more than chance alone would explain. Which conclusion is best supported?$q$, $q$[{"text":"No conclusion is possible because the students were not a sample survey","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confused-experiment-with-survey"},{"text":"The app improves vocabulary scores for all high school students in the country","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"generalized-beyond-the-sample"},{"text":"The app caused higher scores for students like the volunteers in this study","is_correct":true},{"text":"The study shows only an association, not a cause","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"denied-causation-in-experiment"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The app caused higher scores for students like the volunteers in this study$q$, $q$Random assignment lets the researchers conclude the app caused the difference, but the volunteers were not a random sample of all students, so the result applies to students like them. Claiming it holds for every student in the country generalizes beyond the group studied.$q$, 'draft', null)
