   $q$Keanu measures the reaction times of a random sample of 40 students and gets a sample mean of $51.4$ hundredths of a second. He simulates 200 samples of size 40 from a population modeled on his data; the simulated means are approximately normal with mean $51.4$ and standard deviation $1.8$. Using a margin of error of two standard deviations, which interval estimates the population mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$51.4$ to $55.0$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"added-margin-on-one-side-only"},{"text":"$47.8$ to $55.0$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$49.6$ to $53.2$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-one-standard-deviation"},{"text":"$46.0$ to $56.8$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-three-standard-deviations"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$47.8$ to $55.0$$q$, $q$The margin of error is $2(1.8) = 3.6$, so the interval is $51.4 \pm 3.6$, from $47.8$ to $55.0$. The choice $49.6$ to $53.2$ uses only one standard deviation as the margin.$q$, 'draft', null)
