   $q$Scores in a regional quiz bowl are approximately normal with mean $220$ and standard deviation $30$. A z-table gives $P(Z < 0.5) = 0.6915$. About what score separates the top $30.85\%$ of teams from the rest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$205$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"sign-error"},{"text":"$250$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-one-standard-deviation"},{"text":"$235$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$240.75$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-probability-as-z"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$235$$q$, $q$The top $30.85\%$ means $1 - 0.3085 = 0.6915$ lies below, so $z = 0.5$ and the score is $220 + 0.5(30) = 235$. The choice $205$ subtracts, which would cut off the bottom $30.85\%$ instead.$q$, 'draft', null)
