   $q$A school wants to know whether a later start time causes students to earn higher grades. Which plan would allow a cause and effect conclusion?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Randomly assign volunteer students to the early or later start and compare their grades","is_correct":true},{"text":"Compare this year's grades under the later start with last year's grades","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-before-after-without-control"},{"text":"Survey a random sample of students about whether they would prefer a later start","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confused-survey-with-experiment"},{"text":"Compare the grades of students who chose the later start option with those who did not","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"allowed-self-selection"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Randomly assign volunteer students to the early or later start and compare their grades$q$, $q$Only random assignment makes the two groups alike apart from the start time, so a difference can be credited to the schedule. When students choose their own start time, motivated students may cluster in one group, which is an observational comparison.$q$, 'draft', null)
